IMPORT prelude

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- the amounts: rounding (reg 4); the maximum weekly
-- rate of income compensation (reg 23); no minimum weekly rate (reg 24); board and lodging (regs 25, 26); the wheelchair
-- maximum (reg 34); travel rates (reg 35); the eligible dependent child allowance (reg 65); the funeral expenses maximum
-- (reg 66); interest on sums ordered or agreed (reg 108); the maximum damages for less than 25% impairment (reg 122); the
-- general maximum amount (reg 134). Each indexed amount is subject to s 538(5) of the Act: never varied downwards.
--
-- SEAT: the injured worker (and, for regs 65 and 66, the worker's dependants after the worker's death). Questions are
-- phrased as that person asks them: "What is the most I can be paid ...?", "How much ... this financial year?".
--
-- NUMBERS. The regulations state a starting figure for the financial year beginning 1 July 2024 and a method: vary it by
-- the change in the Perth CPI (March quarter to March quarter) or in the WA Wage Price Index (December quarter to December
-- quarter), and each later year vary the previous year's amount the same way. The index figures and last year's amount
-- are published elsewhere and are not in the deposit, so they are INPUTS; the starting figures and the method are
-- encoded. The "percentage by which the index varies" is taken unrounded (fork F2).
--
-- Edition: Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024, compilation version 00-c0-00, current from 30 June
-- 2026 (mrdoc 49606, retrieved 19 October 2026), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49606.txt.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 19 October 2026, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation and Injury Management Regulations 2024 (WA) -- the amounts`

§§ `reg 4 -- rounding`

-- Reg 4: "An amount worked out under these regulations must be rounded to the nearest whole dollar with an amount that is
-- 50 cents more than a whole dollar being rounded up to the next whole dollar."
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest whole dollar` `amount` MEANS FLOOR (`amount` PLUS 0.5)

-- Reg 35(2): "Despite regulation 4, an amount worked out under subregulation (1) must be rounded to the nearest whole cent
-- with an amount that is half a cent more than a whole cent being rounded up to the next whole cent."
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest whole cent` `amount` MEANS FLOOR ((`amount` TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `the method common to regs 26, 34, 35, 65, 66, 122, 134`

DECLARE `Rounding` IS ONE OF
    `to the dollar`
    `to the cent`

-- "varying the amount ... by the percentage by which the [index] varies from the previous [index]", for the financial year
-- beginning 1 July 2024 from the starting figure, and for each later year from the previous year's amount; s 538(5): "If,
-- for a particular period, variation under the regulations of an adjustable amount would reduce the amount, the amount
-- must not be varied for the period." The regulations begin with the year beginning 1 July 2024 (reg 2): for an earlier
-- year they say nothing.
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER
      `the starting figure` IS A NUMBER
      `last year's amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the later index` IS A NUMBER
      `the earlier index` IS A NUMBER
      `rounding` IS A `Rounding`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` `the starting figure` `or` `last year's amount` `by` `the later index` `over` `the earlier index` `rounded` `rounding` MEANS
    IF `the year the financial year begins` LESS THAN 2024
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: the regulations set no amount for a year before 2024-25)
    ELSE JUST (IF `the later index` AT MOST `the earlier index`
               THEN `the amount before variation`
               ELSE `rounded as required` (`the amount before variation` TIMES `the later index` DIVIDED BY `the earlier index`))
    WHERE
        `the amount before variation` MEANS
            IF `the year the financial year begins` EQUALS 2024
            THEN `the starting figure`
            ELSE `last year's amount`
        GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        `rounded as required` x MEANS
            CONSIDER `rounding`
            WHEN `to the dollar` THEN `rounded to the nearest whole dollar` x
            WHEN `to the cent` THEN `rounded to the nearest whole cent` x

§§ `regs 23, 24 -- income compensation`

-- Reg 23: "the maximum weekly rate of income compensation for a financial year must be calculated by multiplying by 2 the
-- average of the amounts that the Australian Bureau of Statistics published as the all employees average weekly total
-- earnings in Western Australia for pay periods ending in the months of May and November preceding the financial year."
-- Note: s 538(5): never varied downwards, so last year's rate is the floor.
@export What is the most I can be paid in income compensation a week this financial year (reg 23; Act ss 53, 538(5))?
GIVEN `the May average weekly total earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc ABS all employees average weekly total earnings in WA for pay periods ending in the May before the financial year, in dollars
      `the November average weekly total earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The same ABS figure for pay periods ending in the November before the financial year, in dollars
      `last year's maximum weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum weekly rate of income compensation for the previous financial year, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be paid a week` MEANS
    max `last year's maximum weekly rate`
        (`rounded to the nearest whole dollar`
            (2 TIMES ((`the May average weekly total earnings` PLUS `the November average weekly total earnings`) DIVIDED BY 2)))

-- Reg 24: "No minimum weekly rate applies under section 57 if the worker is -- (a) a worker to whom no industrial instrument
-- applies; or (b) a worker to whom no minimum amount applies under the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993."
-- Where neither holds, s 57(7) of the Act has other grounds (board and lodging only, working directors, jockeys), not
-- encoded here.
@export Do the regulations take away my minimum weekly rate of income compensation (reg 24; Act s 57(7)(d))?
GIVEN `an industrial instrument applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, industrial agreement or other industrial instrument applies to your employment
      `a minimum amount applies to me under the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 sets a minimum amount of pay for you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do the regulations take away my minimum weekly rate` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `an industrial instrument applies to me`)
        OR (NOT `a minimum amount applies to me under the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: s 57(7)(a)-(c) of the Act)

§§ `regs 25, 26 -- board and lodging`

-- Reg 26: "the maximum board and lodging daily amount must be calculated by -- (a) for the financial year commencing on
-- 1 July 2024 -- varying the amount of $181 per day by the percentage by which the March CPI varies from the previous March
-- CPI; or (b) for ... each financial year after that -- varying the amount per day for the previous financial year by
-- [the same]". Reg 3: "March CPI, for a financial year, means the CPI for the last March quarter before the financial year".
@export What is the maximum board and lodging daily amount for a financial year (reg 26; Act ss 58(4), 538)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, for example 2026 for 2026-27
      `last year's daily amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum board and lodging daily amount for the previous financial year, in dollars (not used for 2024-25)
      `the March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the last March quarter before the financial year
      `the previous March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the March quarter a year before that
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maximum board and lodging daily amount` MEANS
    `the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` 181 `or` `last year's daily amount` `by` `the March CPI` `over` `the previous March CPI` `rounded` `to the dollar`

-- Reg 25(1): the monetary value of board and lodging "is ascertained by applying the market value of the board and lodging
-- for the period"; (2) market value by reference to "(a) any industrial instrument, contract or agreement that states the
-- value ...; or (b) if the board and lodging is subject to fringe benefit tax -- the taxable value"; (3) "Subregulation (1)
-- does not apply if -- (a) the market value cannot be determined under subregulation (2); or (b) the monetary value ...
-- exceeds the monetary value calculated by taking the number of full days for which board and lodging was provided ... and
-- multiplying it by the maximum board and lodging daily amount"; (4) then it is the full days times that amount.
-- Act s 58(4): the daily amount is the one "applying when the worker's injury occurred".
@export What is the monetary value of the board and lodging my employer provided me over the period (reg 25; Act s 58)?
GIVEN `the market value can be determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an industrial instrument, contract or agreement states the value of your board and lodging, or the board and lodging is subject to fringe benefits tax so that it has a taxable value
      `the market value` IS A NUMBER @desc That stated value or taxable value for the period, in dollars (any number if it cannot be determined)
      `the full days of board and lodging` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of full days in the period for which your employer provided you board and lodging
      `the maximum daily amount when I was injured` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum board and lodging daily amount for the financial year in which your injury occurred, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monetary value of my board and lodging` MEANS
    IF     `the market value can be determined`
       AND `the market value` AT MOST `the cap`
    THEN `the market value`
    ELSE `the cap`
    WHERE
        `the cap` MEANS `the full days of board and lodging` TIMES `the maximum daily amount when I was injured`

§§ `regs 34, 35 -- wheelchair and travel`

-- Reg 34: the maximum for "providing the use of a wheelchair or similar appliance under section 86 of the Act must be
-- calculated by -- (a) for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2024 -- varying the amount of $13 994 by the percentage
-- by which the March CPI varies from the previous March CPI; or (b) ... varying the amount for the previous financial year".
-- Act s 86(1): only where the worker has suffered the loss of, or paralysis of, both legs.
@export What is the most I can be paid for the use of a wheelchair or similar appliance in a financial year (reg 34; Act s 86)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, for example 2026 for 2026-27
      `last year's maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The wheelchair maximum for the previous financial year, in dollars (not used for 2024-25)
      `the March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the last March quarter before the financial year
      `the previous March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the March quarter a year before that
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the wheelchair maximum` MEANS
    `the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` 13994 `or` `last year's maximum` `by` `the March CPI` `over` `the previous March CPI` `rounded` `to the dollar`

-- Reg 35(1): running costs of the worker's vehicle for approved travel are reasonable "if the rate applied is calculated by
-- -- (a) for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2024 -- varying the amount of 55 cents per kilometre by the percentage
-- by which the March CPI varies ...; or (b) ... varying the rate applied for the previous financial year"; (2) rounded to the
-- nearest whole cent.
@export What rate per kilometre for running my vehicle on approved travel is taken to be reasonable in a financial year (reg 35(1), (2); Act s 90)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, for example 2026 for 2026-27
      `last year's rate per kilometre` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate for the previous financial year, in dollars per kilometre, for example 0.57 (not used for 2024-25)
      `the March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the last March quarter before the financial year
      `the previous March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the March quarter a year before that
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the vehicle rate per kilometre` MEANS
    `the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` 0.55 `or` `last year's rate per kilometre` `by` `the March CPI` `over` `the previous March CPI` `rounded` `to the cent`

-- Reg 35(3): meals and accommodation reasonably required for approved travel are reasonable "if the rate applied is
-- calculated by -- (a) for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2024 -- varying the amount of $139 per day by the
-- percentage by which the March CPI varies ...; or (b) ... varying the rate applied for the previous financial year". Reg
-- 35(2) rounds only the subregulation (1) rate to the cent; this one is rounded to the dollar by reg 4.
@export What daily rate for meals and accommodation on approved travel is taken to be reasonable in a financial year (reg 35(3); Act s 90)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, for example 2026 for 2026-27
      `last year's daily rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate for the previous financial year, in dollars per day (not used for 2024-25)
      `the March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the last March quarter before the financial year
      `the previous March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the March quarter a year before that
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the meals and accommodation daily rate` MEANS
    `the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` 139 `or` `last year's daily rate` `by` `the March CPI` `over` `the previous March CPI` `rounded` `to the dollar`

§§ `regs 65, 66 -- after a worker's death (the seat: the worker's dependants)`

-- Reg 65: the eligible dependent child allowance "must be calculated by -- (a) for the financial year commencing on 1 July
-- 2024 -- varying the amount of $149 per week by the percentage by which the WPI varied between the second-last December
-- quarter before the financial year commenced and the last December quarter before the financial year commenced; or (b)
-- ... varying the amount for the previous financial year by [the same]".
@export How much is the weekly allowance for an eligible dependent child of a worker who died, in a financial year (reg 65; Act s 134)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, for example 2026 for 2026-27
      `last year's weekly allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc The allowance for the previous financial year, in dollars a week (not used for 2024-25)
      `the WPI for the last December quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The WA Wage Price Index (ordinary time hourly rates, excluding bonuses, all sectors, original) for the last December quarter before the financial year
      `the WPI for the December quarter before that` IS A NUMBER @desc The same index for the December quarter a year earlier
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the eligible dependent child allowance` MEANS
    `the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` 149 `or` `last year's weekly allowance` `by` `the WPI for the last December quarter` `over` `the WPI for the December quarter before that` `rounded` `to the dollar`

-- Reg 66: the funeral expenses maximum amount "must be calculated by -- (a) for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2024
-- -- varying the amount of $11 739 by the percentage by which the March CPI varies from the previous March CPI; or (b) ...
-- varying the amount for the previous financial year by [the same]".
@export What is the most that can be paid for a deceased worker's funeral in a financial year (reg 66; Act s 135)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, for example 2026 for 2026-27
      `last year's maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The funeral expenses maximum amount for the previous financial year, in dollars (not used for 2024-25)
      `the March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the last March quarter before the financial year
      `the previous March CPI` IS A NUMBER @desc The Perth All Groups CPI for the March quarter a year before that
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the funeral expenses maximum amount` MEANS
    `the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` 11739 `or` `last year's maximum` `by` `the March CPI` `over` `the previous March CPI` `rounded` `to the dollar`

§§ `regs 122, 134 -- the maximum damages and the general maximum amount`

-- Reg 122: the maximum damages for less than 25% impairment, from "$530 724", varied by the WPI as in reg 65.
@export What is the most I can be awarded in damages against my employer if my impairment is less than 25%, in a financial year (reg 122; Act s 424)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, for example 2026 for 2026-27
      `last year's maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum damages amount for less than 25% impairment for the previous financial year, in dollars (not used for 2024-25)
      `the WPI for the last December quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The WA Wage Price Index for the last December quarter before the financial year
      `the WPI for the December quarter before that` IS A NUMBER @desc The same index for the December quarter a year earlier
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maximum damages for less than 25% impairment` MEANS
    `the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` 530724 `or` `last year's maximum` `by` `the WPI for the last December quarter` `over` `the WPI for the December quarter before that` `rounded` `to the dollar`

-- Reg 134: the general maximum amount, from "$252 724" (note 2: it replaces the Act's $243 991, s 566), varied by the WPI.
@export What is the general maximum amount that my compensation limits are built on, in a financial year (reg 134; Act s 538)?
GIVEN `the year the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the financial year begins on 1 July, for example 2026 for 2026-27
      `last year's general maximum amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The general maximum amount for the previous financial year, in dollars (not used for 2024-25)
      `the WPI for the last December quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The WA Wage Price Index for the last December quarter before the financial year
      `the WPI for the December quarter before that` IS A NUMBER @desc The same index for the December quarter a year earlier
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the general maximum amount` MEANS
    `the varied amount for` `the year the financial year begins` `from` 252724 `or` `last year's general maximum amount` `by` `the WPI for the last December quarter` `over` `the WPI for the December quarter before that` `rounded` `to the dollar`

§§ `reg 108 -- interest`

-- Reg 108: the interest payable on a sum ordered to be paid under s 358 or s 359, or agreed to be paid under s 360, of the
-- Act "must be calculated at a rate of 6% per annum". Simple interest for the number of days, on a 365-day year (fork F3);
-- reg 4 rounds the result to the dollar.
@export How much interest is payable to me on a sum ordered or agreed to be paid to me in a dispute, for a number of days (reg 108; Act ss 358-360)?
GIVEN `the sum` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum ordered or agreed to be paid, in dollars
      `the number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days for which interest runs
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest on the sum` MEANS
    `rounded to the nearest whole dollar` (`the sum` TIMES 6 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `the number of days` DIVIDED BY 365)
